msgid "Do you need a native executable?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus on the JVM is already fast, sub-second startup, low memory "
"footprint, and optimized throughput.\n"
"For many applications, JVM mode is the right choice."
msgstr ""

msgid "Native executables shine when:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Startup time is critical*: serverless/FaaS, CLI tools, or scale-to-zero "
"environments where cold starts matter."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Memory is constrained*: dense container deployments or edge devices with "
"tight RAM budgets."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*You want the smallest possible container image*: native binaries produce "
"images under 50MB."
msgstr ""

msgid "JVM mode is typically better when:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Peak throughput matters most*: the JVM's JIT compiler optimizes hot paths "
"at runtime, which can outperform native on long-running workloads."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Build time is a constraint*: native compilation takes minutes, JVM builds "
"take seconds."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*You rely heavily on reflection or dynamic class loading*: these require "
"explicit configuration for native images."
msgstr ""

msgid "Comparing JVM, Leyden AOT, and native modes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Native is one of three runtime options Quarkus supports.\n"
"JVM fast-jar, JVM with xref:aot.adoc[Project Leyden AOT caching] (JDK 24+), "
"and native (Mandrel) each trade cold-start speed, peak throughput, memory "
"footprint, and build cost differently.\n"
"The table below compares them.\n"
"Pick the mode that matches your workload's most important constraint."
msgstr ""

